  "query_preview": "/WEDNESDAY THROUGH MONDAY/...\nIssued at 1213 PM CDT Tue Jul 21 2026\n\nA cooler and less humid airmass will be in place across the \nregion Wednesday into Thursday thanks to todays cold front. \nThis will allow for afternoon highs to be more seasonable with \nlower to middle 80s for central Missouri to the middle and upper\n80s across southern Missouri with a few temperatures around the\n90 mark. With dew points in the 60s, the overall conditions \nwill feel significantly more reasonable than today. \n\nBy Thursday night into Friday, global models flatten the ridge \nas another shortwave trough moves through the area late\nThursday. This will bring the next chances for rain into Friday. \nRain chances continue to be between 30 to 70%, with the highest\npotential across central Missouri. Additionally, a secondary \nwave brings additional rain potential, from 20 to 60%, for \nFriday night into Saturday morning continuing the cooler \nforecast into the start of the weekend. \n\nSynoptic and global models then begin to return the upper level\nridge to the region on Sunday and into early next week setting\nup another round of heat potential. Some of the model 850mb \nforecast temperatures are in the 26 to 28 degree C range for \nnext Monday and Tuesday. This is well in the future, though if \nthis were to pan out, highs could once again climb into the \nmiddle to upper 90s to start next week.",
